**Convention 7.2 (resource and recovery ceiling).** The public scaffold,
block ordering, template, membership table and decoding tables are
installed source-independent data. Their generation, storage and lookup
costs are finite but no useful total-efficiency bound is claimed.
The phase descriptor is actually acquired if requested, and all its
surviving distinctions are counted in (OCC.26). It is not an acquired
reference provided by notation. The full scan can already obtain these
phases; the lower bound does not charge them twice. All unexported
source dependence is isolated by the declared service, not physically
erased for free.

The final temporal factor has $0\le b\le2D$ and $c\in\{0,1\}$,
so $\lceil\log_2(2D+1)\rceil+1$ bits suffice for that factor
alone. Post-request workspace, authentic count input, entry,
authentication, submitted addresses and physical time remain separate.
This deliberately prescribed, nonoptimal code neither bounds the phase
cost of every optimizing code nor determines $M_1(D)$. Its operational
content is exactly recovery of the requested full trajectory, and, for
the prescribed refinement, recovery of all actual gadget phases.

